    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14344#pullrequestreview-5215361359\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks! Plumbing looks fine but I'm less certain on one part below. I think we'll want to brainstorm a bit on how best to integrate into the API/etc.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 624456732,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1789503874
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14344#discussion_r4019873593\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>While I'm not entirely sure how we want to integrate <code>cm-canon-names</code> into the public API here I don't think that this is the way we'll want to do this. We've generally had bad experiences in the past if enabling a feature changes behavior, so I'd prefer to leave this as-is.</p>\n<p>Would you be ok backing out the changes here and in <code>linker.rs</code> below and just landing the plumbing for now?</p>\n</blockquote>",
